Zhiyu local first start

Created configuration, not installed or ACTIVE.
This new environment: __ENV__
Namespace: __NS__
Seed environment ID: __EID__
One operator owner ID: __OWNER__
Loopback ports: PostgreSQL __PG_PORT__, API __API_PORT__, bank __BANK_PORT__.
Never overwrite an old database, runtime, namespace or writer pin.
Templates with null fields / false proof flags are intentionally NOT executable.
No login secret or database password is printed here.
Before writing a command result or an actual request, confirm the destination
file does not exist. On retry keep the old originals and select a fresh suffix.
Do not overwrite an earlier ARM/READ/HANDOFF/SCAN/ACTIVATE response or proof.

A. New cluster and zero opening

Follow README's new Docker Desktop Linux container section. Use ONLY the new
container/volume/image in local-install.json and this postgres.env. Confirm
image, CID, labels, volume and loopback mapping; old resources must not exist.
Use the local Docker engine explicitly. Do not execute these SQL files against
an existing cluster. Do not delete an old volume to make initialization pass.

In PowerShell 7 (replace nothing in these generated path assignments):
$Root = '__ROOT_PS__'
$R = '__RUNTIME_PS__'
Set-Location -LiteralPath $Root
$ZhiyuExe = Join-Path $Root 'bin/zhiyu.exe'
$BankExe = Join-Path $Root 'bin/banksim.exe'
$StartRole = Join-Path $Root 'scripts/Start-LocalRole.ps1'
$Install = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'local-install.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$AppConfig = Join-Path $R 'app-runtime.json'

Wait for the new PG to be ready. Run new-cluster-only.sql through stdin with
psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 as zygo_install_admin on postgres, ONLY new CID.
Then migrate the application:
& $ZhiyuExe migrate -config (Join-Path $R 'migration-runtime.json')
# Stop if native command exit is nonzero.

First bank process, its own foreground terminal:
& $StartRole -Root $Root -Role bank -InitializeBank
# Leave it running. Record its real native PID / creation time / executable.

Another terminal, the same Root/R assignments:
& $ZhiyuExe seed -config (Join-Path $R 'seed-runtime.json')
# Only app zero seed is created. This does NOT initialize bank accounts.
# Stop on failure; never repeat a partial initialization blindly.

Run bank-zero-only.sql through stdin with psql -X -w -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 as
zygo_bank on __ENV___bank, ONLY the same newly verified CID. Expect ZERO_BANK_READY,
one account/one goal and balance_cents 0. No funds, policy or standing authority
is created. Do not feed passwords/DSN as process arguments.

B. Establish the single operator owner through the normal CLI

No writer-pin.json exists yet. A fresh missing control is a compatibility state,
not an ACTIVE fenced writer. Never manufacture a control row directly in SQL.
Read first:
& $ZhiyuExe recovery-control -config $AppConfig -recovery-request (Join-Path $R 'owner-read.json')

Only the exact WRITER_CONTROL_MISSING result permits the first ARM below.
If a control already exists, stop and inspect; never initial-ARM it again.
& $ZhiyuExe recovery-control -config $AppConfig -recovery-request (Join-Path $R 'owner-arm.json') | Tee-Object -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-arm-result.json')
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'ARM failed; retain original output.' }
$ArmControl = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-arm-result.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
if ($ArmControl.owner_id -ne $Install.owner_id -or $ArmControl.environment_id -ne $Install.environment_id -or $ArmControl.mode -ne 'READ_ONLY' -or $ArmControl.generation -lt 1) { throw 'Unexpected ARM result; do not adopt it.' }
$WriterPin = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'writer-pin.template.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$WriterPin.generation = $ArmControl.generation
$WriterPin | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'writer-pin.json') -Encoding utf8NoBOM

The fixed helper holds the native handle and writes START.json/EXIT.json under
.runtime/processes/<fresh-role-run>. It only starts this Root's known bin/config;
it accepts no arbitrary PID or executable, never kills or forwards extra signals.
In separate foreground terminals (same Root/StartRole assignments), start:
& $StartRole -Root $Root -Role api -Bootstrap
& $StartRole -Root $Root -Role worker -Bootstrap
# These plus the initial bank are three real processes. Normal Ctrl+C is later
# delivered in each role's own console; keep the helper until true native exit.

Now fresh READ using the same actual pin:
& $ZhiyuExe recovery-control -config $AppConfig -recovery-request (Join-Path $R 'owner-read.json') | Tee-Object -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-before-handoff.json')
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'READ failed; do not hand off.' }
$CurrentControl = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-before-handoff.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
if ($CurrentControl.owner_id -ne $Install.owner_id -or $CurrentControl.environment_id -ne $Install.environment_id -or $CurrentControl.mode -ne 'READ_ONLY' -or $CurrentControl.generation -ne $WriterPin.generation) { throw 'Control differs; do not adopt another owner.' }
$HandoffRequest = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-handoff.template.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$HandoffRequest.expected = $CurrentControl
$HandoffRequest | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 6 | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-handoff.json') -Encoding utf8NoBOM
& $ZhiyuExe recovery-control -config $AppConfig -recovery-request (Join-Path $R 'owner-handoff.json') | Tee-Object -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-handoff-result.json')
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'HANDOFF failed; retain state.' }
$HandoffControl = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-handoff-result.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
if ($HandoffControl.owner_id -ne $Install.owner_id -or $HandoffControl.environment_id -ne $Install.environment_id -or $HandoffControl.mode -ne 'RECOVERING' -or $HandoffControl.generation -le $WriterPin.generation) { throw 'Unexpected HANDOFF result.' }
# Same owner UUID, new actual generation. Do not guess generation 2 or 3.

C. Drain before scanning; never manufacture shutdown proof

Normally Ctrl+C bank/API/worker in their own terminals and wait for each real
native exit. Verify PID + creation time + executable, do not kill unknown PIDs.
Do not use the shell's Ctrl+C status as a substitute for a held native handle's
exit code. Confirm no old API/bank listener or outstanding external request.

Only after all three old processes really stopped, preserve old writer-pin and
update generation from the saved actual HANDOFF output:
Copy-Item -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'writer-pin.json') -Destination (Join-Path $R 'writer-pin.initial.json')
$WriterPin.generation = $HandoffControl.generation
$WriterPin | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'writer-pin.json') -Encoding utf8NoBOM

Build proof only from the actual helper EXIT records and fresh local checks.
Do this BEFORE restarting bank. It deliberately stops on ambiguous/missing rows.
Shell Ctrl+C exit is transport state; actual_exit_code in EXIT.json is from the
pre-held native handle. An UNKNOWN/identity-unverified/nonzero result is not proof.

$ArmControl = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-arm-result.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$Rows = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'processes') -Filter 'EXIT.json' -Recurse | ForEach-Object { Get-Content -LiteralPath $_.FullName -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json })
$Stopped = @()
foreach ($RoleName in @('bank','api','worker')) {
 $CandidateExits = @($Rows | Where-Object { $_.role -eq $RoleName -and $_.bootstrap_cycle -and $_.namespace -eq $Install.namespace -and $_.environment -eq $Install.environment -and $_.root -eq $Root -and $_.runtime_dir -eq $R -and $_.owner_id -eq $Install.owner_id })
 if ($CandidateExits.Count -ne 1) { throw 'Missing/ambiguous bootstrap exit. Inspect originals; do not guess latest PID.' }
 $ExitRecord = $CandidateExits[0]
 if (!$ExitRecord.native_handle_held -or !$ExitRecord.identity_verified -or !$ExitRecord.verified_exited -or $ExitRecord.actual_exit_code -ne 0 -or $ExitRecord.pid -lt 1 -or !$ExitRecord.native_creation_filetime_100ns) { throw 'Native exit has not been proved.' }
 if ($RoleName -ne 'bank' -and $ExitRecord.writer_generation -ne $ArmControl.generation) { throw 'Wrong initial generation.' }
 $ExpectedExe = Join-Path $Root $(if ($RoleName -eq 'bank') {'bin/banksim.exe'} else {'bin/zhiyu.exe'})
 if ($ExitRecord.native_exe -ne $ExpectedExe -or $ExitRecord.exe_sha256 -ne (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $ExpectedExe -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant()) { throw 'Known image changed.' }
 $Stopped += [ordered]@{role=$RoleName;pid=$ExitRecord.pid;verified_exited=$true;sha256=$ExitRecord.exe_sha256}
}
$KnownExe = @((Join-Path $Root 'bin/zhiyu.exe'),(Join-Path $Root 'bin/banksim.exe'))
$Live = @(Get-CimInstance Win32_Process | Where-Object { $_.ExecutablePath -and $_.ExecutablePath -in $KnownExe })
if ($Live.Count -ne 0) { throw 'A known local product process is still alive.' }
$Connections = @(Get-NetTCPConnection -ErrorAction Stop | Where-Object { $_.LocalPort -in @($Install.ports.api,$Install.ports.bank) -and $_.State -in @('Listen','Established') })
if ($Connections.Count -ne 0) { throw 'API/bank listeners or requests are not drained.' }
$DockerHost = 'npipe:////./pipe/dockerDesktopLinuxEngine'
$Format = '{"id":{{json .Id}},"running":{{json .State.Running}},"image":{{json .Config.Image}},"ports":{{json .HostConfig.PortBindings}},"mounts":{{json .Mounts}},"install":{{json (index .Config.Labels "zhiyu.install")}}}'
$Container = docker.exe --host $DockerHost inspect --format $Format $Install.container | ConvertFrom-Json
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0 -or !$Container.running -or $Container.image -ne $Install.postgres_image -or $Container.install -ne $Install.environment -or @($Container.mounts).Count -ne 1 -or $Container.mounts[0].Name -ne $Install.volume) { throw 'New local PostgreSQL identity differs.' }
$Binding = $Container.ports.'5432/tcp'
if (@($Binding).Count -ne 1 -or $Binding[0].HostIp -ne '127.0.0.1' -or $Binding[0].HostPort -ne [string]$Install.ports.postgres) { throw 'PostgreSQL mapping differs.' }
docker.exe --host $DockerHost exec $Container.id pg_isready -U zygo_install_admin -d postgres
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'This PostgreSQL is not ready.' }
$Proof = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'quiescence.template.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$Proof.processes = $Stopped
$Proof.checked_at = [DateTimeOffset]::UtcNow.ToString('o')
$Proof.all_registered_processes_stopped = $true
$Proof.bank_process_stopped = $true
$Proof.external_requests_drained = $true
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'quiescence.json')) { throw 'Keep old proof; choose a new filename and update the activation template.' }
$Proof | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 8 | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'quiescence.json') -Encoding utf8NoBOM
# These flags now follow verified old native exits and actual current socket/PG
# observations. Proof expires in ten minutes; a later system sleep needs fresh
# observations. This is not a claim about an unrelated environment.

Restart bank normally in its foreground terminal, WITHOUT migration flags:
& $StartRole -Root $Root -Role bank

With the actual new-generation pin, perform a fresh namespace scan:
& $ZhiyuExe recovery-control -config $AppConfig -recovery-request (Join-Path $R 'owner-scan.json') | Tee-Object -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-scan-result.json')
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'SCAN failed; remain RECOVERING.' }
$Scan = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-scan-result.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
if ($Scan.state -ne 'READY' -or $Scan.missing_users -ne 0 -or $Scan.orphans -ne 0 -or $Scan.mismatches -ne 0 -or $Scan.unresolved -ne 0 -or $Scan.state_mismatches -ne 0) { throw 'SCAN not complete; do not activate.' }
$ActivateRequest = Get-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-activate.template.json') -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$ActivateRequest.run_id = $Scan.run_id
$ActivateRequest | ConvertTo-Json | Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-activate.json') -Encoding utf8NoBOM
& $ZhiyuExe recovery-control -config $AppConfig -recovery-request (Join-Path $R 'owner-activate.json') | Tee-Object -LiteralPath (Join-Path $R 'owner-active-result.json')
# ACTIVATE must succeed within 30 seconds of SCAN. If stale, retain it and make
# a new normal scan/proof; do not edit old time, re-ARM or manufacture success.

D. Daily run (after an actual ACTIVE result)

Bank already runs with the normal flags above. Four other foreground terminals:
& $StartRole -Root $Root -Role api
& $StartRole -Root $Root -Role worker
& $StartRole -Root $Root -Role native-standing
& $StartRole -Root $Root -Role projection
Open http://127.0.0.1:__API_PORT__ in Edge. The local session code is in this
private demo-seed.json. Nothing sends it to an external service. First open has
one zero account/goal; no historical/credit/asset/model fixtures or permissions
are generated. Optional source/provider features remain unconfigured.

For normal controlled shutdown, first make a fresh READ, verify same owner and
full control, fill owner-read-only.template.json.expected with that exact object,
then normal READ_ONLY through the CLI. Stop/wait the actual role processes and
stop only this install's container; keep its volume. Do not re-ARM an existing
install or use a copied generation/control from another namespace.
